": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GAFsdnV9mMTBHXimgizWMG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2. payments-worker has recovered, but payments-api is still unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n\n**What I found:** There's no service called \"payments.\" Two payments services were unhealthy, both at an 18% error rate:\n- **payments-worker** was on v3.4.0, marked unhealthy. Its last healthy production release is v3.3.0.\n- **payments-api** was on v5.1.0, marked degraded. Its last healthy production release is v5.0.0.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. **payments-worker:** Rolled back to v3.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The approver signed off, and it's now healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n2. **payments-api:** I also tried to roll this back to v5.0.0, but the approver denied it: \"Wrong service: the problem is in payments-worker.\" No change was made.\n3. **Incident:** Opened SEV2 INC-0001 for payments-worker, which paged on-call. It says root-cause analysis of v3.4.0 is needed before it's redeployed, and it notes the payments-api situation.\n\n**Needs attention:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate, even after the worker recovered. Either it's a separate problem or it just hasn't recovered yet. Someone should decide whether it needs its own rollback to v5.0.0 or a separate investigation. I haven't made any further changes to it.", "type": "text"}]}]}